{"id":"word:hebrew:H842","type":"word","title":"אֲשֵׁרָה","subtitle":"H842 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Asherah (or Astarte) a Phoenician goddess; also an image of the same","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֲשֵׁרָה (H842) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 40 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֲשֵׁרָה (ʼăshêrâh) means Asherah (or Astarte) a Phoenician goddess; also an image of the same First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 14 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֲשֵׁרָה","transliteration":"ʼăshêrâh","pronunciation":"ash-ay-raw'","strong":"H842","lemmaId":"hebrew:H842","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-f","forms":["וַ/אֲשֵׁרִ֑ים","הָ/אֲשֵׁרִ֖ים","הָ/אֲשֵׁרָ֖ה","הָ/אֲשֵׁרָ֥ה","אֲשֵׁ֣רֵי/הֶ֔ם"],"morphs":[["HTd/Np",18],["HNp",6],["HC/Td/Np",4],["HC/Np/Sp3mp",3],["HC/Np",2],["HRd/Np",2],["HNp/Sp3mp",1],["HR/Np",1],["HC/Rd/Np",1],["HNp/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Asherah (or Astarte) a Phoenician goddess; also an image of the same","usage":"grove. Compare 6253 .","full":"H842. Asherah אֲשֵׁירָה אֲשֵׁרָה, 2Kin 17:16 proper name, feminine Ashera (Assyrian proper name, feminine Aš-ra-tu , with sign for deity, in Canaanitish proper name Abad-Ašratum, servant of A. Schr ZA 1888, 363 , compare Wkl & Abel Thontafelfund see El Amarna ii. No. 77, 1. 9, & Sayce RP2. ii. 67, iii. 71 ; on derivatives compare Assyrian aširat , adjective feminine gracious , COT Gloss ): **see now also GFM EB ASHERAH Dr Deut 16:21 Allen DB ASHERAH , all doubtful as to Canaanite goddess Asherah; question left open by Zim KAT 3. 436 ff. (on Semitic goddess Aširtu-Ašratu Id. ib, 432 ff. ); but see Jerem AT im Licht d. Alten Orients 207 (name of goddess Aširat in letter found at Taanach by Sellin (1902-3) and Id. ib. 37. 237 ) (Oppenheim's find at Ras el-`Ain in Mesopotamia, stone shaft with veiled head as top, supposed to identify post with goddess ; if 2Kin 23:7 refers to draped Asherim [see on text Benz Bur], this even more plausible), Id. ib. 23, 208 f. 236 . On pictorial representations of Asherah +? AJSL xix.l (Oct.1902) . — usually with the article: probably a. a Canaanitish goddess of fortune & happiness; having prophets 1Kin 18:19 , an image 15:13 2Chr 15:16 ; 2Kin 21:7 , sacred vessels 23:4 , houses 23:7 . b. a symbol of this goddess, a sacred tree or pole set up near an altar 1Kin 16:33 ; 2Kin 13:6 ; 17:16 ; 18:4 ; 21:3 ; 23:6 , 15 ; prohibited Deut 16:1 ; burnt by Gideon Judg 6:25-26 , 28 , 30 . Plural אֲשֵׁרוֺת a. the goddess 3:7 (probably error for ᵑ9 עַשְׁתָּרֹת ). b. sacred trees or poles 2Chr 19:3 ; 33:3 ; elsewhere אֲשֵׁרִים id. Isa 27:9 12 t.; suffix Micah 5:14 5 t.; — Exod 34:13 (J) Deut 7:5 ; 12:3 ; Isa 17:8 ; 27:9 ; Jer 17:20 ; Micah 5:13 ; 1Kin 14:15 , 23 ; 2Kin 17:10 ; 23:14 ; 2Chr 14:2 ; 17:6 ; 24:18 ; 31:1 ; 33:19 ; 34:3-4 , 7 . — (compare also Sta ZAW 1881, 344 f. RS Semitic i. 171 f., 175 n. We H 235 , who think ׳א only the sacred pole.)","rootNote":"or אֲשֵׁירָה ; from 833 ; happy ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 14 15","keyReferences":["1Kgs 14 15","1Kgs 14 23","1Kgs 15 13","1Kgs 16 33","1Kgs 18 19","2Chr 14 2","2Chr 15 16","2Chr 17 6"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":40,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 14 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲשֵׁ֣רֵי/הֶ֔ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 14 23","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/אֲשֵׁרִ֑ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Np"},{"reference":"1Kgs 15 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":15,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ/אֲשֵׁרָ֑ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Np"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 33","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֲשֵׁרָ֑ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Np"},{"ref